  "id": "mao",
  "term": "MAO",
  "definition": "MAO, or monoamine oxidase, is an enzyme found in mitochondrial membranes that breaks down naturally occurring monoamines. It helps regulate the metabolism of neurotransmitter-related chemicals such as catecholamines and serotonin, and in the liver it also helps inactivate monoamines circulating in the body, including tyramine absorbed from the gut.",
